---

## 2. Basic Encoding and Decoding

Lateralus provides straightforward helper functions for encoding strings and byte slices into standard Base64.

```lateralus
use std.encoding.base64

fn main() {
    let original = "Hello, Lateralus!"
    let encoded = base64.encode_string(original)
    print("Encoded: " + encoded)

    let decoded = base64.decode_string(encoded).unwrap()
    print("Decoded: " + decoded)
}
```

---

## 3. RFC 4648 Test Vectors

Here are the standard RFC 4648 test vectors runnable in Lateralus:

```lateralus
use std.encoding.base64

fn run_rfc_vectors() {
    assert(base64.encode("".as_bytes()) == "")
    assert(base64.encode("f".as_bytes()) == "Zg==")
    assert(base64.encode("fo".as_bytes()) == "Zm8=")
    assert(base64.encode("foo".as_bytes()) == "Zm9v")
    assert(base64.encode("foob".as_bytes()) == "Zm9vYg==")
    assert(base64.encode("fooba".as_bytes()) == "Zm9vYmE=")
    assert(base64.encode("foobar".as_bytes()) == "Zm9vYmFy")
    print("All RFC 4648 test vectors passed successfully!")
}
```

---

## 4. URL-Safe Base64 and Custom Configurations

For web and URL identifiers where `+` and `/` characters are problematic, use URL-safe base64 encoding:

```lateralus
use std.encoding.base64

fn main() {
    let data: [u8] = vec![0xFF, 0xFE, 0xFD, 0xFC]
    let url_enc = base64.encode_url_safe(&data)
    print("URL-safe: " + url_enc)

    let url_dec = base64.decode_url_safe(&url_enc).unwrap()
    assert(url_dec == data)
}
```
